body:
Review findings addressed in 0d3907c:
1. the off-origin test puts G54 on the bar's axis (3, -2) - the machine spindle is the bar's axis; the laws state the field revolves about the fitted axis, which generation guarantees is the spindle (P0 #62, its own PR);
2. LatheSweep::of refuses by name a chord off one meridian plane (MERIDIAN_TOL 1e-6 mm); simulate_lathe_about checks every chord before cutting, so a refusal writes nothing; parting past centre still cuts;
3. new leaned-axis parity case (10 deg about Y, off-origin) exercising the general window reach;
4. laws state the nose circle is the whole modelled solid;
5. dedicated refusal text for a non-lathe tool on a turning op.
Tests: stock_lathe 7/7 (3 new), sim stock_sim lib 25/25, app lathe_field_sim 6, stock_play 7, stock_sim_document 9, stock_view 4; clippy -D warnings clean.
